
   QFront v1.0.0 Change History
   ============================================================================
   pcbirc crew — 2026
   github.com/verta1878/pcbirc

   v1.0.0 (August 2026) — Clean-room release for PCBoard 15.4
   ============================================================================

   This is a complete clean-room rewrite. No code from the original
   QFront v1.20a was used. All protocol support was written from the
   public FidoNet Technical Standards (FTS/FSC) documents.

   Programs:
     QFRONT.EXE    Main mailer (889 lines)
     QFCONFIG.EXE  Configuration editor (720 lines)
     QSCAN.EXE     EchoMail tosser/scanner (848 lines)
     QNLIST.EXE    Nodelist compiler (624 lines)
     QFUTIL.EXE    Utility program (162 lines)

   Core modules:
     session.c     FidoNet session manager — outbound + inbound (960 lines)
     zmodem.c      Zmodem file transfer (795 lines)
     serial.c      Serial port abstraction — FOSSIL/UART/POSIX/Win32 (650 lines)
     emsi.c        EMSI handshake protocol FSC-0056 (467 lines)
     modem.c       AT command modem control (463 lines)
     xmodem.c      Xmodem/Xmodem-1K/XmodemCRC (481 lines)
     events.c      19-flag event scheduler (432 lines)
     bso.c         BSO outbound scanner FTS-5005 (469 lines)
     wazoo.c       YooHoo session handshake FTS-0006 (352 lines)
     nodelist.c    Nodelist parser FTS-5001 (367 lines)
     frequest.c    File request processor (330 lines)
     semaphore.c   Multi-node semaphore management (339 lines)
     route.c       NetMail routing engine (299 lines)
     tic.c         TIC file processor (190 lines)

   Total: 21 source files, 10,123 lines, GPLv3.

   Platforms:
     DOS4G (OpenWatcom 2.0) — 5 binaries in bin/dos/
     Linux (GCC) — 5 binaries in bin/linux/

   Features:
     - PCBoard integration via BOARD.BAT errorlevels
     - EMSI + YooHoo + FTS-1 inbound handshake detection
     - Zmodem + Xmodem file transfer
     - Full BSO outbound scanner with flavour priority
     - 19-flag event scheduler
     - Wildcard routing rules
     - File requests with magic filenames and limits
     - EchoMail tosser/scanner with dupe detection
     - Areafix robot (subscribe/unsubscribe via netmail)
     - Nodelist compiler with nodediff support
     - Multi-node semaphore locking
     - TIC file processing
     - Full-screen TUI configuration editor

   Bugs fixed (9 from original binary analysis):
     BUG-1  No signal handler — Ctrl-C left ports open, locks orphaned
     BUG-2  No SIGPIPE handling — broken pipe crash on serial write
     BUG-3  BSO scan didn't handle .PNT subdirectories for points
     BUG-4  Flow file parse didn't handle ^ and # directives correctly
     BUG-5  Zmodem CRC-32 table had endianness issue on big-endian
     BUG-6  EMSI timeout wasn't applied to DAT packet receive
     BUG-7  Nodelist parser choked on "Boss" keyword (pointlists)
     BUG-8  .BSY lock used fopen() — TOCTOU race with other nodes
     BUG-9  QNLIST had no rollback on CRC failure after nodediff apply

   ============================================================================
   Original QFront v1.20a was by Rob Kittredge / RoCo Software (2000).
   ============================================================================
